              x: ['*Israel’s beauty was the glory and strength it had while Jehovah blessed it. In 607 B.C.E. Jerusalem and the temple were destroyed. Since the heavens are far above the earth, Isaiah 55:9, falling from heaven to earth pictures a dramatic humbling.', 'Verse 1 also says Jehovah did not remember his footstool. David spoke of the ark and the temple as God’s footstool, 1 Chronicles 28:2 and Psalm 132:7. Even the sacred house could not protect a nation that had turned away from him.', 'Jesus used similar language at Matthew 11:23, asking if Capernaum would be lifted up to heaven and then saying it would come down to the Grave. Privileges and reputation do not keep us safe. Only continued faithfulness keeps us in Jehovah’s favor.']
