            { id: 'p1', label: '¶ 1', prompt: 'Why the good news must reach many languages', scriptures: ['Rom 10:13, 14', 'Gen 11:6-9', 'Rev 7:9, 10, 14'], c: {
              s: ['*People need to hear about Jehovah in their own language.', 'At Babel, Jehovah gave people different languages.', 'Jehovah wants people from every language to be his friends.'],
              h: ['*Romans 10:14 asks how people can call on Jehovah if they never hear about him, so they need the message in a language they understand.', 'At Babel, Jehovah mixed up the languages, but now he is gathering a great crowd from all languages, Revelation 7:9.', 'People must call on Jehovah’s name to be saved, Romans 10:13.'],
              x: ['*Romans 10:13, 14 reasons step by step: to call on Jehovah, people must have faith; to have faith, they must hear; to hear, someone must preach. A message in an unfamiliar language cannot build faith, as 1 Corinthians 14:9 shows.', 'At Babel, Jehovah confused the language of proud people who defied him, Genesis 11:7-9. Now he is gathering humble people out of those same language groups. What was once a sign of judgment has become a display of his mercy, Revelation 7:9.', 'Zephaniah 3:9 foretold that Jehovah would give the peoples a pure language so that all could call on his name and serve him shoulder to shoulder. Whatever tongue we speak, Bible truth unites us in worship, and translation helps make that possible.']
            }},
            { id: 'p2', label: '¶ 2', prompt: 'What Zechariah foretold', scriptures: ['Zech 2:11', 'Zech 8:23'], c: {
              s: ['*Zechariah said many people would come to worship Jehovah.', 'People from many nations want to be with Jehovah’s people.', 'What Zechariah said is coming true today.'],
              h: ['*Zechariah 8:23 says ten men from all languages will take hold of a Jew’s robe because they know God is with him.', 'Zechariah 2:11 says many nations would join themselves to Jehovah.', 'We see this prophecy coming true as people of every language join the congregation.'],
              x: ['*Zechariah 8:23 pictures ten men grabbing the robe of a Jew because they have heard God is with him. In the Bible, ten often stands for earthly completeness. So the prophecy suggests that people from all nations, not just a few, would join in Jehovah’s worship.', 'Ruth the Moabite is an early example. She told Naomi that Naomi’s people would be her people and Naomi’s God her God, Ruth 1:16. Likewise, people from many nations today stay close to Jehovah’s people because they see that God is with them.', 'Zechariah prophesied after the return from Babylon, when the Jews were few and discouraged. The promise that many nations would join them, Zechariah 2:11, showed that Jehovah’s purpose reached far beyond their small group. We now see it on a global scale.']
            }}
